r/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T14:05:48-07:00","id":1199825,"title":"","content":"After reading the Geist Development Blog, I feel the Reapers remind me of a few different things:<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Hollows and Soul Reapers from Bleach, mostly because they're ghosts who obtain monstrous powers by donning a mask that robs them of some of their personality and individuality. Further, they act as agents ferry souls of the departed to a supposed afterlife and enforcers of a Status Quo.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Apostates from Berserk, since they have their powers granted to them by a malevolent force that approaches them the moment they've hit rock bottom (figuratively), while passing themselves off as so kind of Messianic agents with benevolent goals.<br /> <br /> Another interesting one they make me think of are Shadows (As presented in Persona 5), since they act as masked servants of a wicked tyrant.<br /> <br /> \u200bLastly would be (And this might seem like a stretch) CP9 from One Piece, being the at times covert enforcers of a corrupt government.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}